id: pm-ts-starter-codeql-dot-contract
title: Make the CodeQL tracker exclusion contract load-bearing
description: "Separate follow-up found while reviewing checkout credentials. In test/ci-tiers.test.ts, Node path.matchesGlob skips leading-dot components for **. Removing !.agents/pm/** from either push or pull_request patterns still leaves the synthetic tracker item excluded in the reducer. Require ordered include/exclude/re-include assertions or a GitHub-compatible matcher, with a mutation regression removing the tracker exclusion, while preserving executable inclusion assertions. The published workflow currently has the exclusion; this is a contract gap."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[3]: ci,follow-up,"gh:unbraind/pm-ts-starter#217"
created_at: "2026-11-16T11:56:02.328Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T02:22:50.070Z"
author: codex-sol-root
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-18T02:22:45.849Z",codex-sol,"Round BP PRRT_kwDOSZpwFM64vN5r: delivered by 2c1415ba (verified at 8274adf). In test/ci-tiers.test.ts, “path filters include dot directories and apply exclusions and re-inclusions in order” verifies dot-directory ordering, and “CodeQL skips prose but includes executable tracker changes in every template” verifies that removing !.agents/pm/** fails the tracker exclusion contract for push and pull_request, for both the root workflow and backend template. All 12 tests in the file passed."
